[[ ## query ## ]]
Provide a summary of the plot of the movie "Back to the Future" in exactly 3 paragraphs, with each paragraph having a title wrapped in double curly braces, i.e. {{title}}. At the end of your response, please explicitly add a postscript starting with P.S.:

[[ ## response ## ]]
{{The Unexpected Journey}}
Marty McFly is a teenager living in 1985 who inadvertently travels back to 1955 after testing a plutonium-powered DeLorean time machine invented by his eccentric friend, Dr. Emmett Brown. Upon arriving in the past, Marty accidentally prevents his parents from meeting, which puts his own existence in jeopardy as he begins to fade from a photograph he brought with him. He must track down the younger version of Doc Brown to devise a plan to fix the timeline.

{{Restoring the Timeline}}
To ensure his parents fall in love and safeguard his future, Marty navigates the social dynamics of 1955 high school life while dealing with the bully Biff Tannen. He orchestrates a romantic encounter at the school's Enchantment Under the Sea dance, carefully balancing the need to bring his father and mother together against the ticking clock of his fading memory. Meanwhile, Doc Brown constructs a complex system to harness the energy of a lightning strike to power the DeLorean.

{{The Return Home}}
With the help of the precisely timed lightning strike, Marty manages to jump back to 1985 just moments before his past self disappears into the time stream. He returns to find that his efforts have significantly improved his family's lives, as his parents are now successful and confident individuals. Reunited with Doc Brown, who had secretly survived the encounter with Libyan terrorists, Marty realizes the profound impact of his temporal interference before heading off on new adventures.

P.S.: This film remains a landmark of 1980s cinema, celebrated for its tight script and memorable performances.

